}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 3-15 rows x 3-15 cols, black background
  foreground_colors: 2-5 distinct non-black colors
  objects: 8-connected monochromatic non-black components
  containers:
    count: 1-2 per grid
    area: 7-21 pixels; bbox 3-6 rows x 3-9 cols, concentrated on observed archetype sizes 3x3, 4x4, 4x5, 4x7, 5x5, 6x6, and 6x9
    fill_ratio: 0.25-0.78 (area / bbox_area); sparse loose U/C-like outline, not solid
    shape: eval-like asymmetric container/cup silhouette; mostly one-pixel-thick crooked outline with occasional 2-pixel-thick bends or short bars
    avoid: generic rectangular U frames, centered symmetric cups, arbitrary random blobs, and long full-width bars except when matching an observed archetype
    bboxes do not overlap with each other [observed]
  contained (inner) objects:
    each sits inside exactly one container's bbox, different color, strictly smaller area
    every pixel lies in the container's concavity, with same-row/same-column container pixels on 3 of the 4 cardinal sides
    area: 1-4 pixels; no pixel overlap with container
    count per container: 1-2; total across grid 1-3
  standalone (distractor) objects:
    count: usually 0-2; rare dense case up to 9, matching eval's single cluttered large example
    area: usually 1-3 pixels; rare larger distractor up to 11 pixels
    bbox NOT contained by any larger different-color object
    may touch a container from the outside, but all pixels stay outside every container concavity; objects do not straddle inside/outside of a U shape
    may share color with contained objects (key distractor pattern)
  transform: erase (recolor to black) every object whose bbox is fully contained in a larger different-color object's bbox; keep everything else

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size and 2-5 foreground colors; assign 1-2 as container colors
    2. Place 1-2 container objects by sampling eval-like U/C silhouette archetypes (fill ratio 0.25-0.78) with non-overlapping bboxes; this is the output state
    3. Optionally place sparse standalone distractor objects: normally 0-2 small specks, with only occasional large-grid dense cases; include occasional outside-adjacent negatives that touch a container but stay fully outside its concavity; ensure no accidental full bbox containment between any pair
    4. For each container, generate 1-2 small inner objects (area 1-4, different color, smaller area) wholly on black cells in the container's three-sided concavity; add them to get the input
    5. Verify solver reproduces output from input (inner objects erased, everything else unchanged)
```
